  "verbalization": "Arundinol B is shown to have a target relationship with SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and 3-Bromo-4-(2,3-Dibromo-4,5-Dihydroxybenzyl)-5-Methoxymethylpyrocatecol. All these compounds ultimately target DMS-273, suggesting a potential pathway where Arundinol B may exert its effects through a shared mechanism on SNU-387, which is then targeted by multiple compounds. The evidence suggests that SNU-387 may be a key intermediate in the interaction between Arundinol B and DMS-273, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear. The presence of multiple compounds targeting SNU-387 implies that the pathway may involve a complex network of molecular interactions, possibly involving signaling pathways or metabolic processes that are not yet fully characterized. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Arundinol B may interact with SNU-387 in a manner that influences DMS-273, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mechanism.",
